menu "WebRTC Classic example"

    config APP_VIDEO_USE_FILE_FRAMES
        bool "Stream sample H.264 frames from SPIFFS instead of camera"
        default n
        help
            On real ESP hardware, webrtc_classic captures live frames from
            the camera (and audio from the mic). For QEMU runs there's
            neither — instead loop through /spiffs/samples/frame-*.h264
            (and the matching Opus frames) via media_stream's
            file-based capture interface. Same WebRTC pipeline, just a
            different frame source.

            Default off; the docker integration test enables this via
            sdkconfig.defaults.qemu so the QEMU master actually has
            something to send to the Python viewer.

endmenu
